      "text": "Let $x$ be a real number, $x > 1.$  What is\n\\[\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}}?\\]\nNote that\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} = \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{2 \\cdot 2^n} - 1}.\\]Therefore,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{(x^{2 \\cdot 2^n} - 1)} \\\\\n&= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^{n + 1}}}{(x^{2^{n + 2}} - 1)} \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2^1}}{x^{2^2} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^2}}{x^{2^3} - 1} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{x^{2^3}}{x^{2^4} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^4}}{x^{2^5} - 1} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{x^{2^5}}{x^{2^6} - 1} + \\cdots \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2^1}}{2x^{2^2} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^2}}{2x^{2^3} - 1} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{x^{2^3}}{2x^{2^4} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^4}}{2x^{2^5} - 1} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{x^{2^5}}{2x^{2^6} - 1} + \\cdots \\\\\n&= \\left(\\frac{x^{2^1}}{2x^{2^2} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^2}}{2x^{2^3} - 1}\\right) + \\frac{x^{2^3}}{2x^{2^4} - 1} \\\\\n&\\quad + \\left(\\frac{x^{2^4}}{2x^{2^5} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^5}}{2x^{2^6} - 1}\\right) + \\cdots \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{2^1}}{2x^{2^2} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^2}}{2x^{2^3} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^3}}{2x^{2^4} - 1} + \\cdots \\\\\n&\\quad + \\frac{x^{2^4}}{2x^{2^5} - 1} + \\frac{x^{2^5}}{2x^{2^6} - 1} + \\cdots \\\\\n&= \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{2x^{2^n} - 1}.\n\\end{align*}Thus, by telescoping,\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \\frac{x^{2^1}}{2x^{2^1} - 1} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{\\frac{x^2}{2x - 1}}.\n\\end{align*}. The answer is \\frac{x^2}{2x-1}",
